# Wave H.r — Operator review BEM

## Problem

Wizard **review step** chrome still emits Denali-branded BEM while sibling datetime/calendar chrome is already `operator-*`:

| Family | Examples |
| ------ | -------- |
| Review shell | `.denali-review`, `__hero`, `__section`, `__photo-grid`, `__gear-*` |
| Validation panel | `.denali-review-validation`, `__issue-link`, `__group-title` |

These are operator wizard presentation hooks under `body[data-workspace-plugin="denali"]` — not product identity.

## Decision

Rename **CSS class tokens only** (TSX `className` + `wizard-review.css` + theme specs):

| Before | After |
| ------ | ----- |
| `denali-review` (+ `__*` / `--*`) | `operator-review` |
| `denali-review-validation` (+ `__*` / `--*`) | `operator-review-validation` |

**Do not rename** in this wave:

- Files / modules (`denali-review-step.tsx`, `denali-review-test-ids.ts`, …)
- Exports (`DenaliReviewStep`, `DENALI_REVIEW_*` test ids)
- Field registry keys (`denali-review-publish-status`)

## Out of scope

- `.denali-wizard-composite*` / picker BEMs
- Moving review components out of the Denali package
- Install-graph isolation

## Verify

```bash
rg 'className=.*denali-review|\.denali-review' \
  packages/workspaces/denali/src packages/workspaces/denali/theme \
  --glob '!**/*.generated.*'
# expect empty
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wave-h-operator-review-bem.spec.ts \
  test/denali-wizard-theme.spec.ts \
  test/denali-review-step.spec.ts
```
